# LF everywhere, in the repository and in every working tree.
#
# `text=auto` lets Git detect text files and normalise them to LF on commit; `eol=lf` checks them
# back out as LF on all three platforms rather than converting to CRLF on Windows. Binary files are
# still detected and left alone.
#
# This matters for more than tidiness: Visual Studio and `dotnet sln` write .sln files with CRLF,
# so without this rule the solution file flips line endings every time either of them touches it,
# producing whole-file diffs that hide the one line that actually changed.
#
# Note this governs *this repository's* files only. The .sln that dotnet-isolate itself generates
# is deliberately CRLF (SolutionFile.fs), matching what `dotnet sln add` produces for whatever repo
# the tool is run against.
* text=auto eol=lf
